                     <description>If set to 1, enables aging function for the write channel of the port. Programming Mode: Static</description>
                     <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WR_PORT_URGENT_EN</name>
                     <description>If set to 1, enables the AXI urgent sideband signal (awurgent). When enabled and awurgent is asserted by the master, that port becomes the highest priority and co_gs_go2critical_wr signal to DDRC is asserted if enabled in PCCFG.go2critical_en register. Note that awurgent signal can be asserted anytime and as long as required which is independent of address handshaking (it is not associated with any particular command). Programming Mode: Static</description>
                     <bitOffset>13</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WR_PORT_PAGEMATCH_EN</name>
                     <description>If set to 1, enables the Page Match feature. If enabled, once a requesting port is granted, the port is continued to be granted if the following immediate commands are to the same memory page (same bank and same row). See also related PCCFG.pagematch_limit register. Programming Mode: Static</description>
                     <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PCTRL_4</name>
               <description>Port n Control Register</description>
               <addressOffset>0x750</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>PORT_EN</name>
                     <description>Enables AXI port n. Programming Mode: Dynamic</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PCFGQOS0_4</name>
               <description>Port n Read QoS Configuration Register 0</description>
               <addressOffset>0x754</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>RQOS_MAP_LEVEL1</name>
                     <description>Separation level1 indicating the end of region0 mapping; start of region0 is 0. Possible values for level1 are 0 to 13 (for dual RAQ) or 0 to 14 (for single RAQ) which corresponds to arqos. Note that for PA, arqos values are used directly as port priorities, where the higher the value corresponds to higher port priority. All of the map_level* registers must be set to distinct values. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>RQOS_MAP_REGION0</name>
                     <description>This bitfield indicates the traffic class of region 0. Valid values are: - 0: LPR - 1: VPR - 2: HPR For dual address queue configurations, region 0 maps to the blue address queue. In this case, valid values are: 0: LPR and 1: VPR only. When VPR support is disabled (UMCTL2_VPR_EN = 0) and traffic class of region0 is set to 1 (VPR), VPR traffic is aliased to LPR traffic. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>RQOS_MAP_REGION1</name>
                     <description>This bitfield indicates the traffic class of region 1. Valid values are: - 0 : LPR - 1: VPR - 2: HPR For dual address queue configurations, region1 maps to the blue address queue. In this case, valid values are - 0: LPR - 1: VPR only When VPR support is disabled (UMCTL2_VPR_EN = 0) and traffic class of region 1 is set to 1 (VPR), VPR traffic is aliased to LPR traffic. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PCFGQOS1_4</name>
               <description>Port n Read QoS Configuration Register 1</description>
               <addressOffset>0x758</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>RQOS_MAP_TIMEOUTB</name>
                     <description>Specifies the timeout value for transactions mapped to the blue address queue. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>11</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>RQOS_MAP_TIMEOUTR</name>
                     <description>Specifies the timeout value for transactions mapped to the red address queue. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>11</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PCFGWQOS0_4</name>
               <description>Port n Write QoS Configuration Register 0</description>
               <addressOffset>0x75C</addressOffset>
               <resetValue>0x00000E00</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_LEVEL1</name>
                     <description>Separation level indicating the end of region0 mapping; start of region0 is 0. Possible values for level1 are 0 to 13 which corresponds to awqos. Note that for PA, awqos values are used directly as port priorities, where the higher the value corresponds to higher port priority. All of the map_level* registers must be set to distinct values. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_LEVEL2</name>
                     <description>Separation level2 indicating the end of region1 mapping; start of region1 is (level1 + 1). Possible values for level2 are (level1 + 1) to 14 which corresponds to awqos. Region2 starts from (level2 + 1) up to 15. Note that for PA, awqos values are used directly as port priorities, where the higher the value corresponds to higher port priority. All of the map_level* registers must be set to distinct values. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>4</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_REGION0</name>
                     <description>This bitfield indicates the traffic class of region 0. Valid values are: 0: NPW, 1: VPW. When VPW support is disabled (UMCTL2_VPW_EN = 0) and traffic class of region 0 is set to 1 (VPW), VPW traffic is aliased to NPW traffic. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_REGION1</name>
                     <description>This bitfield indicates the traffic class of region 1. Valid values are: 0: NPW, 1: VPW. When VPW support is disabled (UMCTL2_VPW_EN = 0) and traffic class of region 1 is set to 1 (VPW), VPW traffic is aliased to NPW traffic. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>20</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_REGION2</name>
                     <description>This bitfield indicates the traffic class of region 2. Valid values are: 0: NPW, 1: VPW. When VPW support is disabled (UMCTL2_VPW_EN = 0) and traffic class of region 2 is set to 1 (VPW), VPW traffic is aliased to NPW traffic. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>24</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PCFGWQOS1_4</name>
               <description>Port n Write QoS Configuration Register 1</description>
               <addressOffset>0x760</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_TIMEOUT1</name>
                     <description>Specifies the timeout value for write transactions in region 0 and 1. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>11</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WQOS_MAP_TIMEOUT2</name>
                     <description>Specifies the timeout value for write transactions in region 2. Programming Mode: Quasi-dynamic Group 3</description>
                     <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>11</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>SARBASE0</name>
               <description>SAR Base Address Register n</description>
               <addressOffset>0xF04</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>BASE_ADDR</name>
                     <description>Base address for address region n specified as awaddr[UMCTL2_A_ADDRW-1:x] and araddr[UMCTL2_A_ADDRW-1:x] where 'x' is determined by the minimum block size parameter UMCTL2_SARMINSIZE: (x=log2(block size)). Programming Mode: Static</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>SARSIZE0</name>
               <description>SAR Size Register n</description>
               <addressOffset>0xF08</addressOffset>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>NBLOCKS</name>
                     <description>Number of blocks for address region n. This register determines the total size of the region in multiples of minimum block size as specified by the hardware parameter UMCTL2_SARMINSIZE. The register value is encoded as number of blocks = nblocks + 1. For example, if register is programmed to 0, region will have 1 block. Programming Mode: Static</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>8</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
         </registers>
      </peripheral>
      <peripheral>
         <name>UDPHSA</name>
         <version>6227160</version>
         <description>IP_Name</description>
         <groupName>UDPHS</groupName>
         <prependToName>UDPHS_</prependToName>
         <baseAddress>0xE0814000</baseAddress>
         <addressBlock>
            <offset>0</offset>
            <size>0x380</size>
            <usage>registers</usage>
         </addressBlock>
         <interrupt>
            <name>UDPHSA</name>
            <description>USB Device High Speed A</description>
            <value>136</value>
         </interrupt>
         <registers>
            <register>
               <name>CTRL</name>
               <description>UDPHS Control Register</description>
               <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
               <resetValue>0x00000200</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>DEV_ADDR</name>
                     <description>UDPHS Address (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>7</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>FADDR_EN</name>
                     <description>Function Address Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>FADDR_ENSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>FADDR_EN_0</name>
                           <description>The device is not in Address state (read), or only the default function address is used (write).</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>FADDR_EN_1</name>
                           <description>The device is in Address state (read), or this bit is set by the device firmware after a successful status phase of a SET_ADDRESS transaction (write). When set, the only address accepted by the UDPHS controller is the one stored in the UDPHS Address field. It will not be cleared afterwards by the device firmware. It is cleared by hardware on hardware reset, or when UDPHS bus reset is received.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EN_UDPHS</name>
                     <description>UDPHS Enable</description>
                     <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EN_UDPHSSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EN_UDPHS_0</name>
                           <description>UDPHS is disabled (read), or this bit disables and resets the UDPHS controller (write). Switch the UHPHS to UTMI.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EN_UDPHS_1</name>
                           <description>UDPHS is enabled (read), or this bit enables the UDPHS controller (write). Switch the UDPHS to UTMI.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>DETACH</name>
                     <description>Detach Command</description>
                     <bitOffset>9</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>DETACHSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DETACH_0</name>
                           <description>UDPHS is attached (read), or this bit pulls up the DP line (attach command) (write).</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DETACH_1</name>
                           <description>UDPHS is detached, UTMI transceiver is suspended (read), or this bit simulates a detach on the UDPHS line and forces the UTMI transceiver into Suspend state (Suspend M = 0) (write).</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>REWAKEUP</name>
                     <description>Send Remote Wake-up (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>10</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>REWAKEUPSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>REWAKEUP_0</name>
                           <description>Remote Wake-up is disabled (read), or this bit has no effect (write).</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>REWAKEUP_1</name>
                           <description>Remote Wake-up is enabled (read), or this bit forces an external interrupt on the UDPHS controller for Remote Wake-up purposes.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>PULLD_DIS</name>
                     <description>Pulldown Disable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>11</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>FNUM</name>
               <description>UDPHS Frame Number Register</description>
               <addressOffset>0x4</addressOffset>
               <access>read-only</access>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>MICRO_FRAME_NUM</name>
                     <description>Microframe Number (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>FRAME_NUMBER</name>
                     <description>Frame Number as defined in the Packet Field Formats (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>11</bitWidth>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>FNUM_ERR</name>
                     <description>Frame Number CRC Error (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>31</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>IEN</name>
               <description>UDPHS Interrupt Enable Register</description>
               <addressOffset>0x10</addressOffset>
               <resetValue>0x00000010</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>DET_SUSPD</name>
                     <description>Suspend Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>DET_SUSPDSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DET_SUSPD_0</name>
                           <description>Disable Suspend Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DET_SUSPD_1</name>
                           <description>Enable Suspend Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>MICRO_SOF</name>
                     <description>Micro-SOF Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>MICRO_SOFSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>MICRO_SOF_0</name>
                           <description>Disable Micro-SOF Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>MICRO_SOF_1</name>
                           <description>Enable Micro-SOF Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>INT_SOF</name>
                     <description>SOF Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>INT_SOFSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>INT_SOF_0</name>
                           <description>Disable SOF Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>INT_SOF_1</name>
                           <description>Enable SOF Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>ENDRESET</name>
                     <description>End Of Reset Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>ENDRESETSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>ENDRESET_0</name>
                           <description>Disable End Of Reset Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>ENDRESET_1</name>
                           <description>Enable End Of Reset Interrupt. Automatically enabled after USB reset.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>WAKE_UP</name>
                     <description>Wake Up CPU Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>5</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>WAKE_UPSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>WAKE_UP_0</name>
                           <description>Disable Wake-up CPU Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>WAKE_UP_1</name>
                           <description>Enable Wake-up CPU Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>ENDOFRSM</name>
                     <description>End Of Resume Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>6</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>ENDOFRSMSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>ENDOFRSM_0</name>
                           <description>Disable Resume Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>ENDOFRSM_1</name>
                           <description>Enable Resume Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>UPSTR_RES</name>
                     <description>Upstream Resume Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>UPSTR_RESSelect</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>UPSTR_RES_0</name>
                           <description>Disable Upstream Resume Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>UPSTR_RES_1</name>
                           <description>Enable Upstream Resume Interrupt.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_0</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 0 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>8</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_0Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_0_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_0_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_1</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 1 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>9</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_1Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_1_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_1_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_2</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 2 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>10</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_2Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_2_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_2_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_3</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 3 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>11</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_3Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_3_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_3_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_4</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 4 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>12</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_4Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_4_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_4_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_5</name>
                     <description>Endpoint 5 Interrupt Enable (cleared upon USB reset)</description>
                     <bitOffset>13</bitOffset>
                     <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
                     <writeConstraint>
                        <useEnumeratedValues>true</useEnumeratedValues>
                     </writeConstraint>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <name>EPT_5Select</name>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_5_0</name>
                           <description>Disable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>0</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>EPT_5_1</name>
                           <description>Enable the interrupts for this endpoint.</description>
                           <value>1</value>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EPT_6</name>
